{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b18d272f-2ae4-414f-ac34-98b29caab6eb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87d2d56e20356100","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-r33s780v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E002.md","content":"# Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing\nfrom the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server\ntopology, before the operator implementation is committed to a design. The answer determines\nthe HTTPRoute design and whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate\nartifact operations — i.e. whether additional server-side work exists beyond the\nflag-composition change. It has bounded outcomes: ingress-level routing only (no server\nchange), or server-side delegation configuration required.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Design and evaluate how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n  dedicated artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's existing Helm-in-operator\n  pattern (MLflow CR spec → Helm values → embedded chart templates → Server-Side Apply).\n- Determine whether path-based routing at the HTTPRoute/ingress layer alone is sufficient, or\n  whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations\n  to the dedicated instance; record the selection with rationale.\n- Sketch the HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's\n  existing conditional creation of Gateway API resources based on runtime CRD discovery.\n- Record the decision so the operator implementation scope is determined, including which\n  conditional branch of downstream work applies.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented routing design for artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the\n  dedicated artifacts-only instance, evaluated against the operator's existing chart rendering\n  and conditional HTTPRoute patterns.\n- A recorded determination, with rationale, of whether the tracking server needs a\n  configuration change to delegate artifact operations (ingress-level routing only vs.\n  server-side delegation), identifying which downstream work the selection implies.\n- The HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance is sketched and consistent with\n  conditional CRD discovery for optional dependencies.\n- The decision record is complete enough that the operator split-server topology work can be\n  planned directly from it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nThis investigation does not directly cover a High Level Requirement; it gates the epic that\nimplements HLR-6 (main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\nartifacts-only instance, P1) and shapes HLR-5's deployment design (P1). It resolves the\nstrategy's open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing from the\nmain tracking server to the dedicated artifacts-only instance?\" (Owner: MLflow Team).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":77212,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d484210dda7c67","agent_id":"acf985de57b4e149a","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"a478b787-602e-4305-8154-08a7589ea1b9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:43:45.867Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
