{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9c47c1c7-1156-434b-9526-23c4837287d9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a67a2caaa10bbd36","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-r33s780v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Audit telemetry channel for workspace access denials\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves which telemetry channel workspace access denials in artifact\nserving should generate audit events through — server logs (the baseline required by the P2\nHigh Level Requirement), OTLP telemetry, or the Kubernetes audit log — and therefore the scope\nof the audit logging implementation. It is a product/security decision requiring PM/Security\ninput, recorded as a decision the audit logging work is gated on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Evaluate the candidate telemetry channels for workspace access denial audit events\n  (server log, OTLP, Kubernetes audit log) against the strategy's requirements: what\n  identity, artifact path/experiment, and denial reason must be captured, and consistency\n  with the tracking server's existing observability surface.\n- Record the PM/Security decision on the channel (or channel set), with the rationale and\n  the stakeholder input captured.\n- Determine the resulting scope of the audit logging requirement: the server-log baseline\n  per the P2 High Level Requirement, plus any additional channel work if selected; channels\n  not selected are explicitly declined.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The telemetry channel decision for workspace access denial audit events is documented,\n  with PM/Security input recorded (owner per the strategy: PM/Security).\n- The scope determination for the audit logging requirement is recorded: the server-log\n  baseline plus any additional selected channel work, or an explicit record that server\n  logs only are selected and other channels are declined.\n- The decision record is complete enough that the audit logging implementation can be\n  planned directly from it.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nThis investigation does not directly cover a High Level Requirement; it gates the epic that\nimplements HLR-8 (audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving, P2) and\ndetermines that epic's scope. It resolves the strategy's open question \"Should workspace\naccess denials generate audit events through a specific telemetry channel (OTLP, Kubernetes\naudit log, server log)?\" (Owner: PM/Security).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":77907,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d484210dda7c67","agent_id":"acf985de57b4e149a","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"f461dc23-9ab1-4a57-9c79-4c3443f7a557","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:43:55.670Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
