{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-cada4356-7ab2-492b-bdf6-ad43df77bd66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a58ba73ec797e5eb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-r33s780v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E004.md","content":"# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins: workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution function\ncorrectly in the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model\nregistry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides experiment-to-workspace\nmapping for the tracking server's non-artifact operations; this epic verifies that resolution\nin the artifacts-only context and, per the feasibility investigation's findings, extends or\nrefactors it (factoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within\nthe plugin if it is coupled to full tracking server initialization). No new plugin flag or\nentry point is introduced — the workspace-aware behavior emerges from the server combining\nits existing flags.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify and extend the plugin's workspace resolution so it initializes and resolves\n  experiment-to-workspace mapping in an artifacts-only server context, without tracking store\n  or model registry store initialization.\n- If the feasibility investigation finds coupling to the full tracking server initialization\n  path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the\n  plugin, keeping the tracking server's existing behavior unchanged.\n- Preserve the existing experiment-to-workspace mapping behavior for the tracking server's\n  non-artifact operations (no regression).\n- Implement a fail-closed resolution contract: when the workspace store cannot be reached or\n  a request's workspace context cannot be resolved, resolution returns a deny/indeterminate\n  result rather than allowing the request — consistent with the strategy's fail-closed\n  posture and reusing the existing auth plugin infrastructure without dictating Kubernetes\n  API mechanics.\n- Make the updated plugin consumable by the MLflow server image build (version\n  pinned/updated in the build requirements), consistent with how the plugin is consumed\n  today (PyPI package, hermetic Konflux build of the MLflow image).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Tests demonstrate workspace resolution initializing and resolving experiment-to-workspace\n  mapping in an artifacts-only context with tracking and model registry stores\n  uninitialized.\n- If coupling was found: workspace resolution runs through an independent initialization\n  path, and the plugin's existing tests for the tracking server context pass unchanged.\n- The tracking server's non-artifact workspace resolution behavior is unchanged (existing\n  test suite passes).\n- The fail-closed contract is verified by test: an unreachable workspace store or\n  unresolvable request yields a deny/indeterminate result, never an allow.\n- The updated plugin is consumable by the MLflow server image build with an updated pinned\n  version.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are\n  validated against workspace membership — this epic supplies the plugin-side workspace\n  resolution the server's validation delegates to.\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only\n  context without tracking store initialization — this epic's primary requirement.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78520,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d484210dda7c67","agent_id":"acf985de57b4e149a","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"56fe292b-6c0a-473c-936c-2bc