tracking deployment; deploy the\n  kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking\n  deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery,\n  consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Add operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations enabling the artifacts-only\n  instance without the workspace flags (misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact\n  requests bypass workspace validation).\n- Preserve current behavior for MLflow CRs that do not enable split-server artifact serving.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciling the CR creates\n  a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main\n  tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the\n  correct flag combinations.\n- The artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` —\n  measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance per the\n  selected routing design — measured end-to-end by artifact requests being served through\n  the dedicated instance.\n- Workspace configuration is propagated to the artifacts-only instance via the same\n  mechanisms as the main tracking deployment, and the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed\n  on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n- HTTPRoute resources are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery (present when\n  Gateway API CRDs exist, absent without error when they do not).\n- The operator rejects MLflow CR configurations that enable the artifacts-only instance\n  without the workspace flags, with a clear validation error.\n- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile identically to current\n  behavior (backwards compatibility).\n- Reconciliation is validated against an MLflow image build that supports the combined\n  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` flags (capability gate; the operator's chart\n  templates reference the flags as configuration and are developed in parallel with the\n  server change).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate\n  Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — this epic's primary requirement.\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n  artifacts-only instance — this epic's routing configuration, per the routing-design\n  investigation's outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":80527,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d484210dda7c67","agent_id":"acf985de57b4e149a","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"77539bf0-eddc-4e1f-a5cf-ad151159f87d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:44:35.052Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
