{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-47945aa8-93d1-4bb3-9d08-846e5c2d5c47","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94cdd535b8e8269c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-r33s780v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E007.md","content":"# Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic implements audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving, so that\ndenied requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are recorded for security\nreview and compliance. The baseline requirement is audit events through server logs; the\ntelemetry channel decision (server log, OTLP, or Kubernetes audit log) determines the final\nscope. The audit hooks instrument the workspace validation path in the server's artifact\nrequest handling.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Emit audit events for workspace access denials in the workspace-aware artifacts-only\n  server's validation path, capturing the requesting identity, the artifact path / parent\n  experiment, and the denial reason.\n- Implement the baseline server-log audit channel per the High Level Requirement, and any\n  additional channel selected by the telemetry channel decision (OTLP or Kubernetes audit\n  log), per that decision's scope determination.\n- Cover both denial classes: workspace membership denials (HTTP 403) and fail-closed denials\n  when workspace validation is unavailable (HTTP 503).\n- Keep successful artifact accesses out of the denial audit stream (denials are the audit\n  subject; do not flood the log with successful requests).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace access denials in artifact serving produce audit events through the decided\n  channel (baseline: server logs) including requesting identity, artifact path / parent\n  experiment, and denial reason — measured by inspecting the emitted events in a\n  multi-tenant test.\n- Both HTTP 403 membership denials and HTTP 503 fail-closed denials generate audit events,\n  each distinguishable by denial reason.\n- Successful artifact accesses do not generate denial audit events.\n- The audit implementation matches the scope determined by the telemetry channel decision\n  (server logs only, or the additionally selected channel).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 (P2): audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server\n  logs — this epic's primary requirement, scoped by the telemetry channel decision.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":81550,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92d484210dda7c67","agent_id":"acf985de57b4e149a","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"ccd6e5ee-fe0d-4422-a95e-1bc1ecc5aaf7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:44:43.111Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
