{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a989e541ebca76f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing\n30\tfrom the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server\n31\ttopology, before the operator implementation is committed to a design. The answer determines\n32\tthe HTTPRoute design and whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate\n33\tartifact operations — i.e. whether additional server-side work exists beyond the\n34\tflag-composition change. It has bounded outcomes: ingress-level routing only (no server\n35\tchange), or server-side delegation configuration required.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Design and evaluate how the main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n40\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's existing Helm-in-operator\n41\t  pattern (MLflow CR spec → Helm values → embedded chart templates → Server-Side Apply).\n42\t- Determine whether path-based routing at the HTTPRoute/ingress layer alone is sufficient, or\n43\t  whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations\n44\t  to the dedicated instance; record the selection with rationale.\n45\t- Sketch the HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance, consistent with the operator's\n46\t  existing conditional creation of Gateway API resources based on runtime CRD discovery.\n47\t- Record the decision so the operator implementation scope is determined, including which\n48\t  conditional branch of downstream work applies.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- A documented routing design for artifact traffic from the main tracking deployment to the\n53\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance, evaluated against the operator's existing chart rendering\n54\t  and conditional HTTPRoute patterns.\n55\t- A recorded determination, with rationale, of whether the tracking server needs a\n56\t  configuration change to delegate artifact operations (ingress-level routing only vs.\n57\t  server-side delegation), identifying which downstream work the selection implies.\n58\t- The HTTPRoute design for the artifacts-only instance is sketched and consistent with\n59\t  conditional CRD discovery for optional dependencies.\n60\t- The decision record is complete enough that the operator split-server topology work can be\n61\t  planned directly from it.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\tThis investigation does not directly cover a High Level Requirement; it gates the epic that\n66\timplements HLR-6 (main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n67\tartifacts-only instance, P1) and shapes HLR-5's deployment design (P1). It resolves the\n68\tstrategy's open question \"How should the operator configure artifact traffic routing from the\n69\tmain tracking server to the dedicated artifacts-only instance?\" (Owner: MLflow Team).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2bd5c6e3d816421","agent_id":"a90bddf3d6b94a5b2","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"44b5dcac-1a83-4aef-9714-8a61544955dc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:47:32.951Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a989e541ebca76f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
