{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b79a8f9b2cfb7c62","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Audit telemetry channel for workspace access denials\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 0\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Audit telemetry channel for workspace access denials\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves which telemetry channel workspace access denials in artifact\n30\tserving should generate audit events through — server logs (the baseline required by the P2\n31\tHigh Level Requirement), OTLP telemetry, or the Kubernetes audit log — and therefore the scope\n32\tof the audit logging implementation. It is a product/security decision requiring PM/Security\n33\tinput, recorded as a decision the audit logging work is gated on.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Evaluate the candidate telemetry channels for workspace access denial audit events\n38\t  (server log, OTLP, Kubernetes audit log) against the strategy's requirements: what\n39\t  identity, artifact path/experiment, and denial reason must be captured, and consistency\n40\t  with the tracking server's existing observability surface.\n41\t- Record the PM/Security decision on the channel (or channel set), with the rationale and\n42\t  the stakeholder input captured.\n43\t- Determine the resulting scope of the audit logging requirement: the server-log baseline\n44\t  per the P2 High Level Requirement, plus any additional channel work if selected; channels\n45\t  not selected are explicitly declined.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- The telemetry channel decision for workspace access denial audit events is documented,\n50\t  with PM/Security input recorded (owner per the strategy: PM/Security).\n51\t- The scope determination for the audit logging requirement is recorded: the server-log\n52\t  baseline plus any additional selected channel work, or an explicit record that server\n53\t  logs only are selected and other channels are declined.\n54\t- The decision record is complete enough that the audit logging implementation can be\n55\t  planned directly from it.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\tThis investigation does not directly cover a High Level Requirement; it gates the epic that\n60\timplements HLR-8 (audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving, P2) and\n61\tdetermines that epic's scope. It resolves the strategy's open question \"Should workspace\n62\taccess denials generate audit events through a specific telemetry channel (OTLP, Kubernetes\n63\taudit log, server log)?\" (Owner: PM/Security).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2bd5c6e3d816421","agent_id":"a90bddf3d6b94a5b2","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"af9008f1-cbd4-4324-a796-0778688a0ea8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:47:33.589Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b79a8f9b2cfb7c62","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
