{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0d5bfb4cf9a8459","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: 'MLflow operator: split-server topology for the dedicated artifacts-only instance'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design investigation selects server-side delegation,\n15\t    the operator scope is rewritten to propagate the delegation configuration to the\n16\t    main tracking deployment (and the branch-B server epic is selected); the HTTPRoute\n17\t    design is otherwise adjusted to the selected routing approach.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MLflow operator: split-server topology for the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic extends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as\n40\ta separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and to configure the main tracking\n41\tdeployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance — a split-server topology in\n42\twhich the main tracking server handles experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt\n43\tregistry while the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace\n44\tvalidation. This is not a single-deployment configuration toggle: it requires new Helm chart\n45\ttemplates and artifact traffic routing configuration, designed per the routing-design\n46\tinvestigation's outcome. Users configure a single MLflow CR; the operator manages the split\n47\ttopology declaratively.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Add Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only instance's Deployment, Service, and\n52\t  HTTPRoute within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec → Helm\n53\t  values → embedded chart templates → Server-Side Apply).\n54\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated\n55\t  artifacts-only instance, per the routing design selected by the routing-design\n56\t  investigation (ingress-level routing, plus propagating any server-side delegation\n57\t  configuration that design requires).\n58\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`,\n59\t  `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration\n60\t  mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment; deploy the\n61\t  kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking\n62\t  deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n63\t- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery,\n64\t  consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n65\t- Add operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations enabling the artifacts-only\n66\t  instance without the workspace flags (misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact\n67\t  requests bypass workspace validation).\n68\t- Preserve current behavior for MLflow CRs that do not enable split-server artifact serving.\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, reconciling the CR creates\n73\t  a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main\n74\t  tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the\n75\t  correct flag combinations.\n76\t- The artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n77\t  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` —\n78\t  measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n79\t- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance per the\n80\t  selected routing design — measured end-to-end by artifact requests being served through\n81\t  the dedicated instance.\n82\t- Workspace configuration is propagated to the artifacts-only instance via the same\n83\t  mechanisms as the main tracking deployment, and the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed\n84\t  on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n85\t- HTTPRoute resources are created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery (present when\n86\t  Gateway API CRDs exist, absent without error when they do not).\n87\t- The operator rejects MLflow CR configurations that enable the artifacts-only instance\n88\t  without the workspace flags, with a clear validation error.\n89\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile identically to current\n90\t  behavior (backwards compatibility).\n91\t- Reconciliation is validated against an MLflow image build that supports the combined\n92\t  `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` flags (capability gate; the operator's chart\n93\t  templates reference the flags as configuration and are developed in parallel with the\n94\t  server change).\n95\t\n96\t## HLR Traceability\n97\t\n98\t- HLR-5 (P1): MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate\n99\t  Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — this epic's primary requirement.\n100\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n101\t  artifacts-only instance — this epic's routing configuration, per the routing-design\n102\t  investigation's outcome.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2bd5c6e3d816421","agent_id":"a90bddf3d6b94a5b2","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"dc7bdd66-cc0a-4024-baa9-5abff4ae26fb","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:47:36.988Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0d5bfb4cf9a8459","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
