{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2e88bfef51769b7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n3\ttitle: Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If PM/Security selects a channel other than server logs (e.g.\n16\t    OTLP or the Kubernetes audit log), the audit implementation is rewritten for the\n17\t    selected channel and its scope determination.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic implements audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving, so that\n40\tdenied requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are recorded for security\n41\treview and compliance. The baseline requirement is audit events through server logs; the\n42\ttelemetry channel decision (server log, OTLP, or Kubernetes audit log) determines the final\n43\tscope. The audit hooks instrument the workspace validation path in the server's artifact\n44\trequest handling.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Emit audit events for workspace access denials in the workspace-aware artifacts-only\n49\t  server's validation path, capturing the requesting identity, the artifact path / parent\n50\t  experiment, and the denial reason.\n51\t- Implement the baseline server-log audit channel per the High Level Requirement, and any\n52\t  additional channel selected by the telemetry channel decision (OTLP or Kubernetes audit\n53\t  log), per that decision's scope determination.\n54\t- Cover both denial classes: workspace membership denials (HTTP 403) and fail-closed denials\n55\t  when workspace validation is unavailable (HTTP 503).\n56\t- Keep successful artifact accesses out of the denial audit stream (denials are the audit\n57\t  subject; do not flood the log with successful requests).\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- Workspace access denials in artifact serving produce audit events through the decided\n62\t  channel (baseline: server logs) including requesting identity, artifact path / parent\n63\t  experiment, and denial reason — measured by inspecting the emitted events in a\n64\t  multi-tenant test.\n65\t- Both HTTP 403 membership denials and HTTP 503 fail-closed denials generate audit events,\n66\t  each distinguishable by denial reason.\n67\t- Successful artifact accesses do not generate denial audit events.\n68\t- The audit implementation matches the scope determined by the telemetry channel decision\n69\t  (server logs only, or the additionally selected channel).\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-8 (P2): audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server\n74\t  logs — this epic's primary requirement, scoped by the telemetry channel decision.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2bd5c6e3d816421","agent_id":"a90bddf3d6b94a5b2","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"e9f8a1ab-35d9-44ab-9d9d-95ada0787f34","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:47:37.579Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2e88bfef51769b7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT