ns\n48\t  to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the routing design selected by the\n49\t  routing-design investigation.\n50\t- Ensure the delegation is driven by configuration propagated by the MLflow operator to the\n51\t  main tracking deployment (the operator renders the main tracking Deployment's\n52\t  configuration), so users still configure a single MLflow CR.\n53\t- Preserve current artifact-serving behavior when the delegation configuration is absent.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The tracking server supports configuration to delegate artifact operations to the\n58\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the selected routing design.\n59\t- Artifact requests to the main tracking server are served via the dedicated artifacts-only\n60\t  instance when delegation is configured — measured end-to-end.\n61\t- Configurations without the delegation setting retain the current artifact-serving\n62\t  behavior (backwards compatibility; rollback is removing the setting).\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated\n67\t  artifacts-only instance — in outcome B this epic delivers the server-side half of that\n68\t  routing, alongside the operator's propagation of the delegation configuration.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2bd5c6e3d816421","agent_id":"a90bddf3d6b94a5b2","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"27e3949a-5466-4c04-84e9-3e35a8fa2d06","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:47:38.233Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b505fb37f3d65609","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
