truction rules and against epic frontmatter:\n39\tE001→E004, E001→E005 (Investigation gates, Rule 3), E004→E005 (library→consumer, Rule 13 — the\n40\tserver's validation builds against the plugin's resolution interface), E002→E006 and E003→E007\n41\t(Investigation gates), E005→E007 (Rule 12/13, serial on the same server validation surface).\n42\tThe mermaid diagram (`graph TD`, dependency→dependent) matches every epic's `dependencies`\n43\tfrontmatter exactly, in both directions, including the dashed E002⇢BRANCH-B-E008 selection edge.\n44\tParallelism is correctly preserved: E005 ∥ E006 (different repos) with the flag-combination\n45\tcoupling expressed as the capability-gate AC on E006, not a DAG edge — the rule-compliant shape.\n46\tE001 ∥ E002 ∥ E003 run as independent roots. The conditional branch file is well-formed:\n47\t`branch: B` matches the filename, `gated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002` is in its direct dependencies,\n48\tand no main-plan epic depends on a branch node. Both bounded outcomes of E002 (ingress-only vs.\n49\tserver-side delegation) are covered, the latter by the branch epic. Critical path 4\n50\t(E001→E004→E005→E007) is reasonable for an M-L strategy with no new components (P0 path is 3).\n51\t\n52\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n53\tComponent naming is handled correctly: \"MLflow Operator\" and \"mlflow-kubernetes-plugins\" have no\n54\tcanonical Jira component, and the summary logs the span to the canonical `MLflow` component with\n55\tper-component rationale rather than inventing names — validator confirms all component values are\n56\tcanonical. All epics are MLflow Team, matching the strategy's single-team scope; the\n57\trepo/surface split (plugin / server / operator) draws the boundaries along the right seams with\n58\tno scope duplication between siblings. The two size overages are managed trade-offs, not\n59\tviolations: E006 (2-3 sprints) and E005 (1-2 sprints) each carry a concrete re-split trigger in\n60\tthe Health Warnings (split criterion named, not a bare planning note). No work-product type\n61\tmixing — no epic bundles code with content authoring.\n62\t\n63\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n64\tAll three Investigations genuinely change downstream structure: E001 decides verify-only vs.\n65\trefactor for E004 and the validation approach for E005; E002 decides E006's scope and the\n66\texistence of BRANCH-B-E008; E003 decides E007's implementation surface. All Implementations\n67\tproduce concrete artifacts. Gating metadata is complete and well-formed on every gated epic:\n68\t`gated_by` targets always appear in the direct `dependencies` list (E004→E001, E005→E001, E006→E002,\n69\tE007→E003, BRANCH-B-E008→E002), every `gated_by` has both `action` and a substantive\n70\t`fallback_approach`, and every Investigation dependency carries `gated_by`. The branch epic's\n71\t`action: remove` with the outcome-A fallback is exactly right.\n72\t\n73\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n74\tSignal fields are type-appropriate everywhere: the three Investigations carry\n75\t`investigation_signals`, all five Implementations carry `ai_signals`, and each has an ai-signals\n76\tfile using the matching rubric. Values were cross-checked against the rubric and the strategy:\n77\tE003's low scores (`source_accessibility: 0`, `human_judgment_required: -2`) correctly reflect\n78\tthat the channel selection is a pending PM/Security decision, while E002's\n79\t`human_judgment_required: 0` is correct because the routing choice is an MLflow-Team technical\n80\tdecision resolvable from readable patterns. E004's `repo_access: 0` is honestly scored and\n81\tconsistent with the Health Warning on the plugin's unverified source. The\n82\t`architecture_claims` calibration was checked against `.context`: both mlflow.md and\n83\tmlflow-operator.md exist and corroborate the cited premises (the kubernetes-auth plugin v1.5.0\n84\tfrom PyPI, `--enable-workspaces`/`--workspace-store-uri kubernetes://`/`--serve-artifacts` in\n85\tDockerfile.konflux, the Helm-in-operator pattern with Server-Side Apply, and conditional Gateway\n86\tAPI CRD discovery) — every Implementation epic scores 1 with a cited, verifiable rationale.\n87\t\n88\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n89\tEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy, including all six proposed strategy ACs\n90\tmapped into E005 and E006 verbatim (HTTP 200/403/503 semantics, distinct Deployment with exact\n91\tcontainer command). Rule-mandated ACs: E005 and BRANCH-B-E008 both carry explicit\n92\tbackwards-compatibility/rollback ACs (omit either flag / remove the delegation setting); the\n93\tkonflux build-pipeline AC is N/A (no onboarding chain — all components already build via\n94\tKonflux); docs-review AC is N/A (no docs-authoring epic, correctly, since Documentation Support\n95\tis \"Pending human review\", not Yes — the Health Warning records the conditional). The\n96\tlatency-measurement AC on E005 is a condition on what the epic itself measures and documents,\n97\tnot an externally-controlled precondition. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID\n98\t(grep confirms the only `E0xx` strings outside the summary are frontmatter dependency entries).\n99\t\n100\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n101\tFull scope coverage: all three affected components have implementation epics; all three SME\n102\toverrides are applied and verified in the epic scopes (no new flag — E005 composes existing\n103\tflags; split deployment, not a config toggle — E006; SSAR mechanics de-specified — E004 states\n104\treuse of the auth plugin infrastructure without dictating Kubernetes API mechanics). All four\n105\tstrategy risks are carried forward (path-resolution ambiguity → E001 scope; plugin coupling →\n106\tE001/E004; split-topology misconfiguration → E006's CR-validation AC; per-request latency →\n107\tE005's measurement AC plus the deferred-caching Health Warning). All four open questions and all\n108\tfive \"needs validation\" assumptions have explicit dispositions in the Open-Question Triage table.\n109\tThe P2 audit HLR is covered, not dropped. Conditional branches cover both stated outcomes of the\n110\trouting question. Strategy-level context (pending process gates, plugin source caveat, design\n111\tdoc/ADR) is surfaced in Health Warnings rather than silently dropped.\n112\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b956a1f9bc167889","agent_id":"a1f4fa653d4ea18c2","session_id":"b73c52d2-9810-4f0f-a474-9e7932db2044","uuid":"74ec2be9-cf02-4eb6-a377-9e817c5a201d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:50:34.792Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a83e97874a074f74","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
